From 0b7d1be16bc3b18253fbad4fbe81ef238622216e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vic Herrera <126992509+vhhr7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:14:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Import external-WAV AAF as editable session data

File > Import > Session Data analyzes an AAF and imports the selected audio
tracks as new tracks, one clip per edit. Clips keep their offset into the
complete source, so handles stay available; the import is one undo step and
Save collects the full sources.

crates/interchange (layer 3, no filesystem/process/UI access):
- build_session(Plan): versioned rational-time plan -> Session. Endpoints are
  rounded to samples independently, so adjacent edits never drift.
- aaf::read_aaf: reads the AAF object model from structured storage with the
  cfb crate (MIT): properties streams, strong reference vectors/sets and
  dictionary weak references. Media goes through a MediaResolver trait.

crates/engine: file.preview_aaf (read-only) and file.import_aaf (undoable).
The resolver opens only files named in the chosen media folder, checks
file_access and reads WAV headers without loading samples; import re-probes
and decodes before touching the session.

crates/ui-egui: Session Data window with track selection, media folder,
absolute/relative mapping, sample offset and report.

Supported: SourceClip/Filler sequences resolved through MasterMobs to
WAVEDescriptor SourceMobs with one external locator; mono/stereo PCM WAV;
composition timecode including 24000/1001 and drop-frame. Gain, fades,
transitions, selectors, nested sequences, embedded essence, split channels,
mixed sample rates and non-local locators fail explicitly.

Addresses #40.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
